    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0085" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3759</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Elkus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-06T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3495. Morgenthau<anchor n="2" xml:id="d16-f1"/> called here yesterday and thought
                    it desirable that you personally have a private interview with Enver and remind
                    him of the cordial feelings the United States entertains for Turkey, and make
                    strong representations of the advantages to Turkey in maintaining friendly
                    relations with this country, and intimate to him that owing to the United States
                    entering into the war the chances of an early peace are greatly improved and the
                    likelihood of German success vastly diminished, and that therefore Turkey should
                    not sever her friendly relations with the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d16-f1" n="2" xml:id="d16-f1-content">
                <p> Henry Morgenthau, former Ambassador in Turkey; retired July, 1916.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
